course: dictionary
lesson: 7127
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Pen is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the clues around the word, which are its context.
explain: «Write your answer in pen, not pencil.» Here pen means a tool for writing with ink. «The farmer put the sheep in the pen by the gate.» Here pen means a small fenced place for animals, and the sheep and gate are the clues.
explain: Pen can also be a verb, which is an action word. «She penned a letter to her gran.» To pen means to write, so try swapping in wrote. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A pen can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action). To pen means to write.
fact: A pen is a tool for writing or drawing with ink.
fact: A pen is also a small fenced place for animals, such as a sheep pen or a pig pen.
fact: Felt-tip pens dry out without a cap because the ink evaporates, which means it slowly goes off into the air.
fact: A pen pal is a friend you write letters to.
exercise: «Write your answer in pen, not pencil.» In this sentence, what is a pen? | A small fenced place for animals | *A tool for writing with ink | A way of counting animals | A friend you write letters to
exercise: «The farmer shut the pigs in the pen.» What does pen mean here? | To write a letter | *A small fenced place for animals | A kind of pencil | A tool for writing
exercise: «She penned a letter to her pen pal.» What does penned mean? | Counted | Lost | *Wrote | Drew a picture
test: Which clue tells you pen means a fenced place in «The sheep were kept in a pen by the gate»? | Letter | *Sheep and gate | Writing | Ink
test: «He penned a note, then put his pen in his pocket.» What does pen mean in the second part? | To write | A friend | *A tool for writing with ink | A fenced place
exam: Lena says pen always means a writing tool. Is she right? | Yes, it never means anything else | Yes, but only in maths | *No, pen can also mean a small fenced place for animals | No, pen means a kind of animal
